WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.634
Hey, let's do some Thank You Notes.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:05.067
James, can I get some Thank You Note writing music, please?

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.501
♪♪

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:07.801
-Speaking of holiday spirit.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.100
-He's always -- Look how happy he is.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.634
-Yeah. Wow.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:13.968
♪♪

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:16.601
-Thank you, last week of the campaign,

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.467
for being when fundraising e-mails switch

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.534
from polite to hostage taker.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:24.067
It's like, "Give me 10 dollars!"

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.200
♪♪

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.467
Thank you, New York City Marathon,

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.801
for being the only time it's a great accomplishment

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.367
to come in 20th place.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.467
Like -- That's pretty amazing.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.601
♪♪

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.968
Thank you, daylight savings time,

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.701
or as Taylor Swift calls you,

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.400
"Midnights (11 pm edition)."

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.167
♪♪

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.200
Thank you, midterm election ads for being the best gig

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.434
in the business for voice actors who say...

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:02.200
[Deep voice] "But is he really who he says he is?"

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.434
[ Ominous music plays ]

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.167
"Is he really?"

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.267
"John Tompkins says he stands for..."

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.033
♪♪

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:18.200
Thank you, Jeff Bezos and Jay-Z

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.667
considering buying the Washington Commanders,

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.501
for being the first time two of the world's richest men said,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.300
"Wanna go halfsies?"

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.868
"Go splitzies on this?"

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:33.868
♪♪

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:37.167
Thank you, bowling balls, for always looking like

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.000
you just found out what your job is.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.901
-"Oh? Ooh?"

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:46.534
"Ooh! Ohh!"

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.133
"Whoa!"

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.834
-Yeah, okay.

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.200
♪♪

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.167
Thank you, letter openers.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.801
Without you, I don't know how anyone

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.133
would be able to barely rip paper.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:04.167
-Get it in the slot.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.968
-Thank you, window caulk, for making it look like

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.734
I'm turning my real house into a gingerbread house.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:12.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.667
Eventually, you'll make it happen.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.033
♪♪

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.234
Thank you, Nespresso Pods,

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.167
for just being acorns from the future.

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:25.300
There you go, everybody. Those are our Thank You Notes.

